# PUPPETEER_SKIP_DOWNLOAD=true — set BEFORE running `pnpm install` in
# network-restricted environments so Puppeteer's postinstall skips the
# Chromium download. It is NOT a runtime env var, so do not add it to a
# runtime .env file — export it in the shell used to install dependencies.
#
# DATABASE_URL — the `postgres` superuser default below is fine for LOCAL
# dev only. The tenant-isolation RLS policies (rls_and_checks.sql) are
# FORCE ROW LEVEL SECURITY, but superusers bypass RLS entirely (a hard
# Postgres limitation), so PRODUCTION must use a dedicated NON-SUPERUSER
# application role here — otherwise every tenant can read every other
# tenant's data. Ideally run migrations as a separate role from the app role.
DATABASE_URL=postgres://postgres:postgres@localhost:5432/vittixbiz
JWT_SECRET=super_secret_jwt_key_here
#
# --- One-time DB role setup (setup-db.ts) -------------------------------------
# These are ONLY needed to run `pnpm db:setup-app-role` — the script that
# creates the restricted, NON-SUPERUSER application role (required for RLS to
# mean anything) and prints the DATABASE_URL to copy into the app's .env. The
# NestJS app itself never reads them, so do NOT put them in the runtime .env
# the app uses — they are run-script-only, like PUPPETEER_SKIP_DOWNLOAD above
# (which is install-time-only).
#
# ADMIN_DATABASE_URL — a superuser/owner connection, the SAME privilege level
# the app must NOT run with. It is used only to create the app role and grant
# permissions, and should be the same role that runs migrations (so the
# ALTER DEFAULT PRIVILEGES it sets apply to future migration objects).
# ADMIN_DATABASE_URL=postgres://postgres:postgres@localhost:5432/vittixbiz
#
# APP_DB_ROLE — name of the restricted application role to create/ensure.
# APP_DB_ROLE=vittixbiz_app
#
# APP_DB_PASSWORD — password for that role. If omitted and the role does not
# exist yet, setup-db.ts generates a strong random one and prints it ONCE.
# If omitted and the role already exists, its existing password is untouched.
# APP_DB_PASSWORD=